      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/nav/overview-md"
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-binary-composition",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.binary-composition",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-binary-composition",
      "layer": "composition",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.composition",
        "medulla.derived-data-lifecycle",
        "medulla.feature-graph",
        "medulla.architecture-gates",
        "medulla.release-composition"
      ],
      "summary": "Feature selection, process lifecycle and the gate suite. Owns the root Cargo.toml feature graph (default = graph, algorithms, metrics, full; full is an 84-entry list that INCLUDES security and the viz family), the five [[bin]] targets each behind required-features (medulla-server/server, nemesis/harness, migrate-shards, restore/redb+server, lake-fixture-export/lake), .cargo/config.toml (target-dir = target-isolated, the GGML CPU portability contract, mold, sccache), arch-lint.toml, the 60-hook .config/pre-commit.yaml and scripts/. It is therefore the owner of every architecture-gate decision: D-MEDULLA-004 (no crate-DAG gate exists), D-MEDULLA-006 (the arch-lint exclude misses target-isolated) and the sequencing half of D-MEDULLA-009."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-cluster-replication",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.cluster-replication",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-cluster-replication",
      "layer": "storage-transaction",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.raft-consensus",
        "medulla.shard-placement",
        "medulla.cross-shard-transaction",
        "medulla.cluster-elasticity"
      ],
      "summary": "The clustering, consensus and replication subsystem (23 modules): node/network/store, membership shrink, drain, reshard, placement, cross-node elasticity, cross-shard transactions, exchange, xread, Pregel, and their harnesses. Like medulla.persistence this seam is entirely absent from the medulla-development skill's layer model, and it is the third-largest AL002 owner. Recorded here so the burndown has an owner."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-composition",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.composition",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-composition",
