      ],
      "summary": "RF-022 layer boundary root seam, carried forward unchanged from the non-authoritative fixture at plans/refactor/architecture/components/medulla.yml. It owns no source path; the implementation components listed in child_component_ids do."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-compute",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.compute",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-compute",
      "layer": "query-reasoning",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.compute-domains",
        "medulla.graph-algorithms",
        "medulla.datalog-reasoning"
      ],
      "summary": "Compute domains: graph algorithms (always compiled), AST/tree-sitter, finance, datascience and Datalog reasoning. Consumed by medulla-query, medulla-epistemic, medulla-plan, medulla-tsdb and (optionally) medulla-kvcache -- the last two are the D-MEDULLA-002 edges."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-core",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.core",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-core",
      "layer": "core",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.graph-invariants",
        "medulla.identity-rbac-admission",
        "medulla.graph-acl-isolation",
        "medulla.graph-policy-lease"
      ],
      "childComponent": [
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-graph-core"
      ],
      "summary": "RF-022 layer boundary root seam, carried forward unchanged from the non-authoritative fixture at plans/refactor/architecture/components/medulla.yml. It owns no source path; the implementation components listed in child_component_ids do."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-embedded-bindings",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.embedded-bindings",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-embedded-bindings",
      "layer": "server-protocol",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.embedded-store",
        "medulla.pyo3-inprocess-binding",
        "medulla.language-clients"
      ],
      "summary": "In-process and out-of-process language bindings: the embedded store surface, the PyO3 in-process binding (opt-in only -- the out-of-process build must never link it, enforced by scripts/check_no_pyo3.sh), the Python client package (governed by .importlinter) and the JS client (governed by clients/js/.dependency-cruiser.cjs, which is the ONLY thing the dependency-cruiser-architecture hook validates -- see D-MEDULLA-004)."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-epistemic",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.epistemic",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-epistemic",
      "layer": "query-reasoning",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.claims-evidence-belief",
        "medulla.contradiction-tms"
      ],
      "summary": "Claims, evidence, belief-state, contradiction detection, confidence propagation and justification (a truth-maintenance system), plus the facade's reasoning cascade and reasoning projection that serve it."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-graph-core",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.graph-core",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-graph-core",
      "layer": "core",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.graph-invariants",
        "medulla.identity-rbac-admission",
        "medulla.graph-acl-isolation",
        "medulla.graph-policy-lease",
        "medulla.rls-view-cache",
        "medulla.semantic-indexing"
      ],
      "summary": "GraphCore (petgraph graph + ledger), GraphRegistry (multi-tenant), isolation.rs (the zero-trust ACL, AccessLevel/RowVisibility/check_access/can_see_row/filter_view and mint_policy_decision_lease), SemanticStore, rls_view_cache.rs and rbac_persist.rs. Per RF-022/RF-010's four-boundary ruling this is the SOLE deciding authority for durable RBAC/identity admission, graph ACL / tenant isolation / row visibility, and policy-decision-lease minting; medulla.query-plan, medulla.persistence and medulla.server-dispatch are consumers that call lease.filter_view()/validate_before/validate_after, never a second deciding authority."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-job-plane",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.job-plane",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-job-plane",
      "layer": "storage-transaction",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.analytics-job-plane",
        "medulla.statechart-engine",
        "medulla.durable-work-item"
      ],
      "summary": "The durable analytics-job plane over a redb-backed AnalyticsJob state machine (committing results as provenance'd claims through GraphCore), plus its disciplined sibling, the formal FSM/statechart engine and its durable machine-instance store. The three facade-level statechart definitions (work item, loop, agent lifecycle) are owned here because they are chart DEFINITIONS over this engine, not server dispatch."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-kv-cache",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.kv-cache",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-kv-cache",
      "layer": "storage-transaction",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.tiered-kv-cache"
      ],
      "summary": "Tiered hot/warm/cold KV-cache store plus the content-addressed shared multi-instance backend. Its edge to medulla-compute is OPTIONAL behind the off-by-default `graph` feature (graph-guided paging) and is NOT in the default or `full` feature closure -- see D-MEDULLA-002."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-lake-interop",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.lake-interop",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-lake-interop",
      "layer": "storage-transaction",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.lakehouse-interop",
        "medulla.sqlite-file-format"
      ],
      "summary": "Foreign storage-format interop: the LTAP lakehouse leg (Parquet + Delta + Iceberg + Iceberg-REST catalog) and the pure-Rust SQLite .db file-format reader/bulk-load writer (no C, no libsqlite3). Both are format adapters with no in-engine store authority; grouped because both exist solely to read and write somebody else's on-disk format."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-lm-program",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.lm-program",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-lm-program",
      "layer": "types",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.lm-program-contract"
      ],
      "summary": "Graph-native governed LM-program and self-improvement contracts (deps = medulla-modality, medulla-types). Contract-only; wired into the facade behind the root `program-optimization` feature. Model- and vendor-agnostic by construction, per the layout contract's prohibition on vendor labels in ownership identity."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-modality",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.modality",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-modality",
      "layer": "types",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.modality-contract",
        "medulla.governed-media-decode",
        "medulla.typed-document-structure",
        "medulla.geospatial-predicates",
        "medulla.lexical-index",
        "medulla.stream-cep",
        "medulla.evidence-alignment",
        "medulla.tensor-modality"
      ],
      "summary": "The ModalityContract seam and every crate that converges on it. medulla-modality owns the trait + conformance harness (TCK) and deliberately sits BELOW medulla-plan/medulla-core with deps = medulla-types only. The leaves own governed pure-Rust decode + evidence: PCM/WAV, PNG + pHash, ISOBMFF + RGB frames, typed document pages/layout/tables, WKT geometry + an in-house packed Hilbert R-tree (no GEOS/PROJ), a Tantivy BM25 inverted index, a bounded-NFA CEP engine, and the shared alignment graph over EvidenceLocus. medulla-tensor is owned here as the dense N-D array modality but carries a declared layer violation (see D-MEDULLA-002): its edge to medulla-tsdb is mandatory while its edge to medulla-modality is OPTIONAL behind the `contract` feature."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-mutation-store",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.mutation-store",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-mutation-store",
      "layer": "types",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.mutation-ledger",
        "medulla.mutation-scope-binding",
        "medulla.private-payload-seal",
        "medulla.store-incarnation-identity",
        "medulla.store-relocation-adoption"
      ],
      "summary": "RF-RULING-004's two dependency-ordered authorities, formerly one crate (medulla-mutation-store, retired 2026-09-06 -- see migration_lineage). medulla-transaction (\"Sole mutation authority: admission, ordering, fencing, commit, replay identity, outbox, and consensus-transaction intent records\") is MutationKernelV1: ledger.rs, admission.rs, commit.rs, saga.rs, replay.rs, the participant/ consensus-transaction intent codec, and its own src/tests/ integration suite. medulla-storage (\"Sole physical-state authority: durable opens, owner-table registry, scoped capabilities, snapshots, backup/restore/adoption, recovery validation\") is StorageKernelV1: the owner/ registry, physical/ manifest+incarnation, recovery/ adopt+backup+validate, and direct_state/ journal. medulla-transaction depends on medulla-storage (StorageKernelV1 hands MutationKernelV1 write authority via a move-once MutationOwnerAuthority); medulla-storage names no medulla-transaction edge, so the physical-state kernel can never depend inward on its mutation-authority consumer. Kept as ONE registry component (see migration_lineage) because both crates implement exactly the five capability_ids this component already owned before the split -- no capability moved, gained, or was lost. Still placed under target layer `types`, NOT `storage-transaction`, for the same cyclicity reason as before the split: medulla-core (layer `core`) depends on both crates."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-numeric-ann",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.numeric-ann",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-numeric-ann",
      "layer": "types",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.numeric-kernel",
        "medulla.ann-index"
      ],
      "summary": "The slim BLAS/LAPACK-free numeric kernel (ndarray + nalgebra; one kernel, two surfaces) and the native IVF-PQ + OPQ + SQ8-refine ANN index built on it. Kept as one seam because medulla-ann is the only in-workspace consumer of medulla-numeric's kernel surface besides the quantum stack, and both are pure numeric leaves with no store or policy authority."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-observability",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.observability",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-observability",
      "layer": "composition",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.metrics-otel",
        "medulla.slow-query-observability",
        "medulla.cost-accounting",
        "medulla.audit-log"
      ],
      "summary": "Metrics, OpenTelemetry export, the slow-query log, cost accounting and probes, the audit log, autosizing and channels, plus the served observability surfaces (obs/, traces/, promql/). Kept disjoint from medulla.server-dispatch's roots so exclusive ownership holds."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-persistence",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.persistence",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-persistence",
      "layer": "storage-transaction",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.storage-transaction",
        "medulla.durable-graph-persistence",
        "medulla.shard-migration",
        "medulla.backup-restore",
        "medulla.cold-tier-offload",
        "medulla.write-coalescing",
        "medulla.agent-library-table"
      ],
      "summary": "The facade's own durable persistence and transaction layer: the 20,818-line crates/medulla-store/src/redb_store.rs graph store plus its submodules (capacity leases, development lane, work-item capability, resource reservations), the redb physical layout, persist locking, durability, mutation apply, the write coalescer, graph deltas, at-rest crypto, and src/server/persistence/ (redb_backend, shard_migrate, backup, cold_offload). This component is NOT modelled anywhere in the medulla-development skill's layer table and owns the single largest AL002 burden in the repository. ADDED 2026-09-12 (F5): the RF-020 Agent Library's durable table also lives here, within the existing `src/server/persistence/` root -- agent_library.rs (3061 lines), agent_component.rs (2064), agent_graph.rs (1907), agent_template.rs (1463), and agent_pin_resolution.rs (570). This was UNCLAIMED as recently as the 5523859a/2026-09-04 verification (\"do not exist in this repository yet\"); see `capability_authority_model.previously_unclaimed_now_claimed` for the correction record. Whether the implementation covers every RF-020 behavior (revisions/outbox/tombstones/replay/reconciliation) is NOT independently re-verified here -- `evidence_status` stays `not_run`."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-quantum",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.quantum",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-quantum",
      "layer": "query-reasoning",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.quantum-contracts",
        "medulla.quantum-simulation",
        "medulla.quantum-hardware-backends",
        "medulla.quantum-job-integration",
        "medulla.quantum-workloads"
      ],
      "summary": "The quantum specialty sub-DAG, six crates, entirely default-off (none of the quantum/quantum-quest/quantum-gpu/quantum-hardware features is in `full`). medulla-quantum-core holds the QuantumProgram IR, the QuantumBackend trait + capability flags, the estimate()/planner rules R0-R5 and the exactness-typed QuantumResult; gates supplies unitary matrices; sim is statevector + stabilizer; hardware adapts IBM/Braket/Azure and is ALWAYS BackendFamily::Hardware, never exact; jobs runs quantum as an medulla-jobs AnalyticsJob; workloads (QAOA) writes back TYPED PROPOSALS through the :Claim/:Evidence/SUPPORTS convention, never a hard constraint. NOTE: the skill says 'Quantum (5)'; there are SIX."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-query-plan",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.query-plan",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-query-plan",
      "layer": "query-reasoning",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.query-reasoning",
        "medulla.cross-modal-planner",
        "medulla.sql-catalog",
        "medulla.wasm-udf"
      ],
      "summary": "The SQL/Cypher surface (DataFusion behind the `sql` feature), the SQL catalog and its native scope key, and THE unified cross-modal planner: a RowSet closed algebra sequencing SQL, graph and vector legs into one plan with cost-based reorder. medulla-plan has the widest fan-in in the workspace (13 path dependencies). medulla-wasm -- the wasmtime-sandboxed UDF runtime with fuel + memory limits and no host capabilities -- is owned here because the plan/query surface is its only consumer."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-query-reasoning",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.query-reasoning",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-query-reasoning",
      "layer": "query-reasoning",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.query-reasoning",
        "medulla.semantic-indexing"
      ],
      "childComponent": [
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-compute",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-query-plan",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-rdf-semantics",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-epistemic",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-quantum",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-viz"
      ],
      "summary": "RF-022 layer boundary root seam, carried forward unchanged from the non-authoritative fixture at plans/refactor/architecture/components/medulla.yml. It owns no source path; the implementation components listed in child_component_ids do."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-rdf-semantics",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.rdf-semantics",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-rdf-semantics",
      "layer": "query-reasoning",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.rdf-sparql",
        "medulla.shape-validation",
        "medulla.graphql-read-surface"
      ],
      "summary": "RDF <-> property-graph mapping and SPARQL 1.1 compiled to GraphView scans, the pure-Rust SHACL Core and ShEx Core validators over medulla-rdf's oxrdf model, and the native GraphQL read surface (schema-from-graph + a resolver compiling to GraphView scans). Grouped as one seam because all four share the oxrdf term/graph model and the GraphView scan contract. Carries an undocumented dev-dependency cycle (medulla-rdf dev-depends medulla-shacl, which depends on medulla-rdf) -- see D-MEDULLA-003."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-server-dispatch",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.server-dispatch",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-server-dispatch",
      "layer": "server-protocol",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.server-protocol",
        "medulla.kg-delegate",
        "medulla.policy-aware-query-dispatch",
        "medulla.wire-protocol-family",
        "medulla.federation",
        "medulla.cdc",
        "medulla.blob-store",
        "medulla.kv-surface",
        "medulla.s3-surface",
        "medulla.obda"
      ],
      "summary": "The root facade's server/protocol adapter and the TOP of the DAG. There is deliberately no medulla-server crate: the server lib and the bin are 1:1, so splitting would carry no consumer and entangle the server/metrics features. Owns dispatch.rs (14,174 lines -- the 'thin routing table' convention describes the intent, not the present state), handlers/, state.rs, auth.rs, access.rs, transport.rs, mutation.rs, mutation_batch.rs, the ten-member wire family (pgwire, mysql_wire, mssql_wire, bolt_wire, redis_wire, sqlite_wire, amqp_wire, mqtt_wire, stomp_wire, broker_wire), federation/, cdc*, s3/, lake/, obda/, blob/ and kv.rs. It is the one permitted caller of IsolationLayer::mint_policy_decision_lease (authorize_and_route_knowledge_stream), enforced by the mint-lease-call-sites hook."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-server-protocol",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.server-protocol",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-server-protocol",
      "layer": "server-protocol",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.server-protocol",
        "medulla.kg-delegate",
        "medulla.policy-aware-query-dispatch"
      ],
      "childComponent": [
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-server-dispatch",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-embedded-bindings"
      ],
      "summary": "RF-022 layer boundary root seam, carried forward unchanged from the non-authoritative fixture at plans/refactor/architecture/components/medulla.yml. It owns no source path; the implementation components listed in child_component_ids do."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-speech-providers",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.speech-providers",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-speech-providers",
      "layer": "types",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.asr-provider",
        "medulla.tts-provider"
      ],
      "summary": "Provider implementations of the frozen `asr.*` and `tts.*` contracts medulla-audio declares. They are the only crates in the workspace that compile a vendored C/C++ library (whisper.cpp/ggml via whisper-rs-sys), which is why the repo's CPU-portability contract (GGML_NATIVE=OFF and the explicit GGML_BMI2=OFF in .cargo/config.toml) exists; the fleet's hosts are pre-AVX2. Providers never decide policy and never own a mutation scope."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-storage-transaction",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.storage-transaction",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-storage-transaction",
      "layer": "storage-transaction",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.storage-transaction",
        "medulla.agent-library-table"
      ],
      "childComponent": [
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-timeseries",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-job-plane",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-kv-cache",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-lake-interop",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-persistence",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-cluster-replication"
      ],
      "summary": "RF-022 layer boundary root seam, carried forward unchanged from the non-authoritative fixture at plans/refactor/architecture/components/medulla.yml. It owns no source path; the implementation components listed in child_component_ids do."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-timeseries",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.timeseries",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-timeseries",
      "layer": "storage-transaction",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.timeseries-store",
        "medulla.timeseries-primitives"
      ],
      "summary": "The native time-series store and its TS primitives (time_bucket / ASOF / gap-fill / OHLC / rollup / decay_weighted_mean). Owns its own native mutation scope. Its crate Cargo.toml states outright that depending on medulla-core AND medulla-compute 'puts medulla-tsdb ABOVE medulla-compute in the DAG -- parallel to where medulla-query sits', which is why D-MEDULLA-002 rules the LAYER assignment wrong rather than the edge."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-types",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.types",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-types",
      "layer": "types",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.contracts",
        "medulla.agent-library-entry"
      ],
      "childComponent": [
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-wire-contracts",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-mutation-store",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-modality",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-numeric-ann",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-lm-program",
        "component/medulla/registry/medulla-speech-providers"
      ],
      "summary": "RF-022 layer boundary root seam, carried forward unchanged from the non-authoritative fixture at plans/refactor/architecture/components/medulla.yml. It owns no source path; the implementation components listed in child_component_ids do."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-viz",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.viz",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-viz",
      "layer": "query-reasoning",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.view-spec-contract",
        "medulla.viz-columnstore",
        "medulla.viz-lod-kernels",
        "medulla.viz-graph-tiles",
        "medulla.viz-export"
      ],
      "summary": "The native visualization stack. medulla-viz-core is the declarative ViewSpec chart IR, the ViewResult exact-vs-approximated metadata, the mark capability matrix and the LOD tier-selection rules -- a true leaf with ZERO normal-build workspace dependencies. Above it: the columnstore, the M4/LTTB kernels (runtime-detected AVX2), graph tiles and export. CORRECTION to the skill: the viz features are NOT all off by default -- `full` (which is in `default`) enables viz, viz-columnstore, viz-static-export, viz-interactive and viz-graph-tiles."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/medulla/registry/medulla-wire-contracts",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "medulla.wire-contracts",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/medulla",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/medulla/component-registry/medulla-wire-contracts",
      "layer": "types",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "medulla.contracts",
        "medulla.mutation-batch-contract",
        "medulla.method-policy-ledger",
        "medulla.durable-execution-routing",
        "medulla.host-resource-capacity",
        "medulla.agent-library-entry"
      ],
      "summary": "The zero- and one-edge contract leaves every other component imports. medulla-types is the BOTTOM of the DAG and the only crate the whole workspace can see: protocol.rs (Request/Response/Method/ResultPayload), types.rs, wire.rs, acl.rs and the MutationBatch v1 contract itself (mutation_batch/, incl. MutationScope, MutationScopeIdentity, PRIVATE_PAYLOAD_EVENT_TYPES, COMPILED_BATCH_INCARNATION and the three domain predicates). medulla-capabilities is the machine-checked MethodPolicy projection of medulla_types::protocol::Method (deps = medulla-types only). medulla-durable carries routing contracts only (CallShape/WorkShape/DurableBackendKind) with no journal, lease or 2PC. medulla-resource is dependency-free cgroup-aware capacity resolution. Grouped as one seam because all four are contract-only, are consumed workspace-wide, and splitting them would produce exactly the tiny-facade pattern the layout contract forbids. ADDED 2026-09-12 (F5): the RF-020 Agent Library identity contract also lives here, still within the existing `crates/medulla-types/src/` root -- `agent_library.rs` (`AgentLibraryEntry`, `AgentLibraryLifecycle`, the schema-versioned definition/tool-surface digest domains, currently v5), `agent_component.rs`, `agent_graph.rs`, and `agent_template.rs`. This was UNCLAIMED as recently as the 5523859a/2026-09-04 verification; see `capability_authority_model.previously_unclaimed_now_claimed` for the correction record."
    },
    {
